+# Dead-code audit report
+
+**Generated:** 2026-09-05
+**Scope:** all 1,193 tracked Python modules
+**Tool:** Vulture 2.16, `--min-confidence 90`
+
+## Summary
+
+The audit found **31 review candidates** after safe, behavior-preserving cleanup. Static analysis cannot reliably determine whether standalone scripts expose functions or options to external callers, so the remaining candidates have **not** been deleted automatically. They are grouped below to make follow-up review safe and actionable.
+
+| Confidence | Candidates | Interpretation |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| 100% | 25 | Unused locals/parameters or unreachable statements detected from control flow. |
+| 90% | 6 | Unused imports; review before removal if an optional dependency has an intended import-time side effect. |
+
+## Safe repairs completed during this audit
+
+The following high-confidence findings were repaired because their behavior was unambiguous:
+
+- `auto_archive.py`: moved the Zstandard compression-level cap before the missing-dependency exception.
+- `7zer.py` and `rmc.py`: restored disk-space summary code so it executes before program exit.
+- `sunik.py`: initialized the non-comment sortable list in the correct branch and handled removed duplicate slots safely.
+- `strip_exif.py`: removed an always-true conditional without changing the image-write path.
+- `dh_reverse.py`: removed diagnostics permanently hidden by `if False`.
+- `urlzz.py`: normalized `str | Path` input before calling `read_text()` and removed an unreachable fall-through return.
+- `extract_base64_assets.py`: removed an unused duplicate-key signature table; the active MIME detector already performs the relevant checks.
+- Removed clear shadowed imports/definitions reported by Ruff, including an obsolete `NameRecord` import in `apk_font_extractor.py`.
+
+## Remaining 100% confidence candidates
+
+| File | Line | Finding | Review guidance |
+| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
+| `auto_comp.py` | 77 | Unused `keep_temp` parameter | Either implement the documented retention behavior or remove the API option. |
+| `check_path_conflicts.py` | 85 | Unused `name_type` parameter | Remove only after confirming external callers do not supply it. |
+| `create_cargo_toml.py` | 82 | Unused `include_dev_deps` parameter | Likely an incomplete feature; implement dev-dependency output or remove the option. |
+| `create_setuppy.py` | 68 | Unused `project_dir_name` parameter | Review intended package-discovery behavior before changing the public helper. |
+| `csshtmlpret.py` | 241–243 | Unused `topdown`, `onerror`, and `followlinks` parameters | The `walk2list` signature appears to retain an older `os.walk`-style API. |
+| `delemp.py` | 179, 206 | Unused `mmap_threshold` parameters | Review whether the threshold should drive the advertised mmap optimization. |
+| `dirinfo.py` | 70 | Unused `chart_type` parameter | Confirm the selected rendering mode is no longer supported. |
+| `find_transliterations.py` | 77 | Unreachable code after `return` | The following heuristic block may be intentional legacy logic; choose either the direct fuzzy-score path or the heuristic path before deleting it. |
+| `fixwhlnames.py` | 59 | Unused `original_filename` local | Safe-looking local cleanup, but retain until output naming behavior is reviewed. |
+| `gextco2.py` | 335 | Unused `is_async` local | Review asynchronous extraction behavior before removal. |
+| `line_analyzer.py` | 33 (two) | Unused `freq_limit` and `low_var_limit` parameters | Potentially incomplete filtering controls. |
+| `pfzf.py` | 183 | Unused `preview_window` parameter | Potentially incomplete UI option. |
+| `pfzf_1.py` | 183 | Unused `preview_window` parameter | Same candidate as the related variant. |
+| `pipget.py` | 122 (two) | Unused `upload_d` and `upload_t` locals | Review package upload metadata handling. |
+| `pp_pdfminer2.py` | 48 | Unused `layoutmode` parameter | Potentially incomplete PDF-layout control. |
+| `pycatimg.py` | 118 | Unused `bg_color` parameter | Potentially incomplete rendering option. |
+| `rename_by_parent.py` | 29 | Unreachable `return None` after an infinite loop | Low-risk removal after confirming the walker’s exhaustion behavior. |
+| `ruimg.py` | 102 | Unused `base_paths` local | Review image-root selection before removal. |
+| `smart_archiver.py` | 169 | Unused `sample_size` parameter | Potentially incomplete sampling optimization. |
